WEBVTT

00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:18,080
I got my blood lab done and the only thing that seemed off to me was the ALT, which was a nine

00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:26,000
in a couple, which was a nine a couple months ago in a 23 last week. Other enzymes were

00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:35,040
my normal, very low, is anything to be concerned about. Well, you know, I don't know. So when you're

00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:41,680
looking at your lab results, what you see in the ranges is the lab ranges. So there's a difference

00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:48,000
between lab ranges and functional ranges. So something could be within normal lab ranges,

00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:54,080
but could be at the high or low end of that lab range would would usually make it out of

00:00:54,080 --> 00:01:02,160
range as far as a functional range. But then you have to look at patterns. So when you look at a lab,

00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:08,000
you look at a functional range, then you look at patterns of what's off, and then you look at

00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:15,840
a previous lab. So you look at trends. So that's how you need to really read a lab report.

00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:24,160
ALT of 23, I believe, still is within the functional range. If everything else was within the lab range,

00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:30,640
again, it could be outside in the functional range. So we'd have to look at the big picture there.

